{
    "article_summary": "This article describes a green radical synthesis of 3,4-dihydropyrimidin-2-(1H)-ones/thiones via a visible-light-induced Biginelli reaction. The process utilizes 4CzIPN, a carbazole-based donor-acceptor fluorophore, as a metal-free photocatalyst in ethanol at room temperature. The reaction proceeds through a proton-coupled electron transfer (PCET) mechanism, offering high yields, short reaction times, and gram-scale applicability.",
